  "verbalization": "Nitrendipine, a calcium channel blocker, is shown to interact with multiple calcium channel subunits, including Cacna1s, Cacnb2, and Cacna1d, all of which are involved in high-voltage-gated calcium channel activity. This suggests that Nitrendipine may modulate calcium influx through these channels, potentially affecting cellular signaling and excitation. The shared involvement of these subunits in the same pathway implies a common mechanism of action, possibly targeting the same or related calcium channels. The evidence supports a role for Nitrendipine in influencing high-voltage-gated calcium channels, which are critical for neuronal and cardiac function. The observed binding to multiple subunits and their shared participation in the same activity suggests a mechanism that could involve channel modulation or regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integrated evidence points to a plausible mechanistic link between Nitrendipine and Cacna1c, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action.",
